<td align="left" width="20px"><b>Answer:</b></td>
<td align="left"><b>fred groth</b> - 20/01/2004 06:43:45
</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>hello there!<br>
i built a rather crude prototype based on a trapped sphere<br>
traveling in an elliptical orbit. i took an aluminum block and cut an egg shaped<br>
channel in it. Then i placed a 1" diameter ball in the channel and covered it with a plexiglass sheet. i then put two holes in the side of the block connected to the channel,<br>
one for air input,one for exhaust. i then applied 130 psi (all i had) to the input port.<br>
the results were interesting. it kind of wiggled from point A to point B, but it did traverse<br>
as expected. like i said it was crude but there are many ways i can <br>
think of to stabilize and increase power. next time i will turn it skyward<br>
and take out some lights in my shop!<br>
<br>
if only i can find the time.....<br>
<br><br></td></tr>
